# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory) and edit it for the machine you are
# on. `.env` is host-specific and should not be committed; this template is.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DAS_ROOT - NOT DECIDED YET.  See docs/OPEN-ITEMS.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The DAS path on the desktop has not been settled, so this is left unset on
# purpose. compose.yaml falls back to ./_das_placeholder when DAS_ROOT is
# empty or absent, which is enough for:
#
#   - docker compose build
#   - the MatUp smoke test on victorian_wood (that example material ships
#     inside the repo, so it is reached through /workspace, not /data)
#
# You must set it before anything touches the MatSynth dataset.
#
# DAS_ROOT is the ONLY host-specific value in the whole workspace. It is
# mounted at /data inside both containers, so every path in configs/ can be
# written once as /data/... and stay valid on any machine.
#
# Windows + Docker Desktop - use forward slashes, and make sure the drive is
# shared under Settings > Resources > File sharing:
#   DAS_ROOT=F:/texsr
#
# Linux:
#   DAS_ROOT=/mnt/das/texsr

#DAS_ROOT=
